[#:seon.task{:name "reader-head-check-is-a-second-declaration-derivation"
             :plan "The reader derives function and test declarations by a top-level head check (function-declaration, test-declaration :306: (first form) resolves to defn/deftest), beside admission's one derivation from clj-kondo's analysis (seon.sci.eval/analyzed-rows -> `seon.fn/source-rows`). Admission never reads these facts (seon.sci.eval/row uses only schema, ns and deletion facts), but seon.turn's read-only-evaluation classifier (turn.clj:2024, `seon.program/declaration-row` over source events) does, so (do (defn f ...)) reads there as declaring nothing. Make that classifier read the evaluation's admitted entity, then delete the reader's function/test head checks. Read `seon.sci.reader/read-events`, `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` and `docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-do-defn-opus-2026-09-26.md`."}
