             :plan "A schema declared by `seon.schema/register!` in an agent namespace stores no `:seon.schema/ns` link: every one of 3390 schema entities on default has none, though `seon.sci.reader/declaration-facts` sets it, program.cljc:1308 copies it and `my.program/names-through` (src/my/program.clj:285) reads it to list a namespace's schemas. Done when `seon.loop-proof-test/virtual-loop-end-to-end` line 'the 4 order schema keys of my.agents.juniper' (test/seon/loop_proof_test.clj, the [?s `:seon.schema/ns` ?n] query) passes: find where the batch/turn path drops the ns (suspect 5e22bc5f6, one path S10) and fix the producer. Read `seon.program/canonical-row`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-value-deeper-than-the-readers-stack-cannot-be-read-back"
             :plan "`seon.id/printed` prints any depth (77c9f5459), but the one reader recurses once per level (edamame parse-next/parse-to-delimiter): a stored value artifact nested deeper than ~2,000 collection levels reads as one error event 'java.lang.StackOverflowError' after a restart, so `seon.render.value/read-artifact` refuses it (3,000-deep vector text on default, 2026-10-07). Make the read depth-safe at its producer (iterative collection reading in the edamame fork, or a declared depth bound the printer and admission share so no unreadable artifact is ever stored). Done when a seon.sci.reader-test regression reads (str (apply str (repeat 10000 \"[\")) (apply str (repeat 10000 \"]\"))) as one form and seon.render.value-test round-trips a 10,000-deep artifact through read-artifact. Read `seon.sci.reader/read`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/spec-reviews/review-deep-opus.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/waste/deep-value-notes.md`."}
