            :plan
            "An agent reply mixing prose and a ```clojure fence evaluates every prose word as a form: 'I will add two numbers, see ``seon.db/q`` for nothing.' answered six 'Unable to resolve symbol' errors, the backticked span as syntax-quote (seon.db/q, clojure.core/for), and '## Next step' as an invalid-token read error; only the fence lines were dropped (agent context-mockups, default at 42e569d9d, 2026-10-07). CLAUDE.md: prose becomes comments. Done when a reply's prose outside fenced clojure blocks reads as comments (Markdown kept as comment text) and only fenced or bare forms evaluate, asserted through the agent entrance. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/context-design/reference-kinds-notes.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/live-run/report.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "name-the-read-event-schema"
             :plan "`seon.sci.reader/read` returns `[:or [:vector :map] :seon.sci.reader/failure]`: the read event is an anonymous `:map`, and no `:seon.sci.reader/event` schema exists (0 holders), so no reference level of `seon.ref/brief` can show the `:seon.sci.reader/error` member with its `:error-kind` (for example `:odd-map`) that an agent needed to fix its form. Only 56% of contracted arities name an output schema (`docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/reflevels-opus.md`, c81161289). Name the event at its producer: register `:seon.sci.reader/event` (an open map; the member carrying `:seon.sci.reader/error` is a named variant of it), declare it as the element of `seon.sci.reader/read`'s output vector, and have its consumers (`seon.turn/read-row`, which reads `:seon.sci.reader/error` from the event, and the no-forms variant `:seon.cluster.reply/no-forms-error`) declare the same name. Proof: to write before assignment (the installed contract of `seon.sci.reader/read` names `:seon.sci.reader/event`, and `seon.ref/brief` of it shows `:seon.sci.reader/error`). Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/reflevels-opus.md`."}

